<HelpTab>
    <HelpSection Title="Typical week">
        <FluentText>
            The grid shows each day of the week against each hour (UK time), averaged over the range. Use
            <strong>Shade by</strong> to choose what the colour shows, and hover a cell for the detail.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Hours to look at">
        <FluentText>Insights flags hours where staffing didn't match demand:</FluentText>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>▲ Busy for the staff on</strong>: at least one and a half times as many games per staff hour as typical.
                Think about adding cover.</li>
            <li><strong>▼ Quiet for the staff on</strong>: half or fewer games per staff hour than typical, with enough people
                on that someone could go home and someone would still be there.</li>
        </ul>
        <HelpNote>
            To avoid flagging one party or one quiet week, nothing is flagged unless the range is at least 14 days
            with at least 30 games. Each hour also needs to have come up at least 3 times, with at least 5 games
            before it can count as busy.
        </HelpNote>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="By part of the day and over time">
        <FluentText>
            <strong>By part of the day</strong> uses the parts of the day from the music schedule, such as "Before opening",
            to total clocked hours and games per staff hour. The charts below show games per day and staff hours
            per day across the range.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
